source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A backslash written as a character reference is not a backslash byte, so the delimiter still opens and Jira renders bold; jiro reads the reference and the bold effect.
-- input.jira --
&#92;*b*
-- rendered.html --
<p>&#92;<b>b</b></p>
-- want.md --
&#92;**b**
-- warnings.json --
[]
